From ee23a972e1af2a1ec3f2eeb5783dac176c589a89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qzshch <qzshch@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:28:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] feat(models): rolling sparse prefill window and
 window-derived capacities

Thread an optional KV working-set window (pages) from --kvmem-window-pages
through EngineOptions, SequencePlanningInputs, and SequencePlanImpl:

- Main and MTP request entitlements clamp to the window plus one prefill
  chunk (Main) or the draft lead (MTP); the Main pool's minimum page count
  follows the window instead of the logical ceiling, so a 256K workspace
  sizes its device pool by the window.
- Admission maps only the first chunk plus the window; each chunk boundary
  (roll_sparse_prefill_window) maps the next chunk's growth, re-derives the
  entitlement, and demotes everything outside the sink prefix plus the
  rolling window (Main and the MTP follower pool share the selection).

Dense operation (window == 0) is byte-identical: the clamps and the roll
call are all gated on the window being set.

